# Production build config for SAiM Mobile (the canonical SAiM surface).
# Committed deliberately: none of these are secrets — the API URL is tailnet-only
# and unreachable without Tailscale. Netlify UI env vars are NOT used for this
# site, so this file is the single source of truth for the production build.
# Secrets (e.g. VITE_VAULT_API_KEY) must never be added here.

VITE_API_URL=https://pi5.tailecb90f.ts.net

# Host guard — if the app is ever served from somewhere else, DeploymentGuard
# shows a blunt error instead of a misleading "offline" state.
# ⚠ BOTH spellings, and the sara.* ones are PERMANENT — not a leftover to tidy.
# Nick's call, 15 Sep 2026: the custom domain STAYS `sara.nickward.co.uk`. The
# Netlify site was renamed `saim-nickward` (so the *.netlify.app host moved) but
# the address people actually use did not, because switching it changes the
# PWA's ORIGIN — Netlify redirects a non-primary domain to the primary, and
# localStorage and IndexedDB are per-origin, so the stored PIN and anything
# unsent in the OUTBOX would be stranded. Not worth spending a capture on a URL.
# Delete these three only if the domain is ever actually moved.
VITE_ALLOWED_HOSTS=saim.nickward.co.uk,saim-nickward.netlify.app,main--saim-nickward.netlify.app,sara.nickward.co.uk,sara-nickward.netlify.app,main--sara-nickward.netlify.app
# ⚠ The host that actually SERVES, not the one the rebrand would imply. This is
# DeploymentGuard's "Open the correct SAiM Mobile site" link, shown when the app
# is loaded from an unrecognised host — so pointing it at saim.nickward.co.uk,
# which has no DNS record, would make the one recovery route a dead end.
VITE_CANONICAL_URL=https://sara.nickward.co.uk
VITE_BUILD_LABEL=prod-mobile
